{"name":"Lakeshore","hex":"#5b96a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lakeshore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a lake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lakeshore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lakeshore, Ontario","blocks":[{"text":"Lakeshore is a municipality on Lake St. Clair, in Essex County, Ontario, Canada. It was incorporated in 1999 by amalgamating the town of Belle River with the townships of Maidstone, Rochester, Tilbury North, and Tilbury West. It is the largest and the most populous municipality within Essex County. However, it is part of the Windsor census metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Lakeshore_ON.JPG/330px-Lakeshore_ON.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lakeshore%2C_Ontario","wikidata":"Q1801144"},{"title":"Lakeshore (provincial electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Lakeshore was a provincial electoral district in Ontario, Canada, that elected members to the Legislative Assembly of Ontario. It was roughly located in southern Etobicoke It existed from 1963 to 1987 when it was abolished into Etobicoke—Lakeshore."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lakeshore_(provincial_electoral_district)","wikidata":"Q6479018"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Lakeshoreseal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Lakeshoreseal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALakeshoreseal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Atlas_Tube_Recreation_Centre_%28SW_View%29_-_Lakeshore%2C_ON.jpg/500px-Atlas_Tube_Recreation_Centre_%28SW_View%29_-_Lakeshore%2C_ON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte